      "explanation": "<p>The one-letter code for each amino acid is as follows:</p>\n<p>Glutamic Acid (A) is represented by the letter E (III).<br/><br/>\nGlutamine (B) is represented by the letter Q (I).<br/><br/>\nTyrosine (C) is represented by the letter Y (IV).<br/><br/>\nTryptophan (D) is represented by the letter W (II).</p>\n<p>These one-letter codes are part of the standard notation used in biology and biochemistry to represent the 20 standard amino acids, plus a few others. The codes are designed to be short and easy to remember, while still being distinct from each other.</p>\n"
